1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:55,700
You're Tops

2
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:58,200
Is that you, Susan?

3
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,200
It's me, Grandpa.

4
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,695
Am I glad to see you!

5
00:01:01,695 --> 00:01:04,500
And am I glad to see you!

6
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:07,700
I am also glad to be here.

7
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:09,439
How are things?

8
00:01:09,439 --> 00:01:11,900
I have been talking to a group of salesmen

9
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:13,400
since ten this morning,

10
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:16,150
and I'm real exhausted.

11
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:18,500
Well, you look good.

12
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:19,500
What's Harry doing tonight?

13
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:19,700
He and Michelle

14
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:22,300
are visiting relatives in New Jersey today.

15
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:24,900
The rest of our family went to the movies.

16
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:27,500
So it's just you and me, Susan.

17
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:30,028
It's nice to be alone with you, Grandpa.

18
00:01:30,028 --> 00:01:31,638
We don't get to see enough of each other.

19
00:01:31,638 --> 00:01:33,400
Oh, I feel the same way, Susan.

20
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,500
I miss seeing you.

21
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,483
But to tell the truth,

22
00:01:37,483 --> 00:01:38,700
next time

23
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:40,300
I'd like to go into the city and meet you there,

24
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:42,900
instead of you coming here.

25
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:44,701
You don't need to do that, Grandpa.

26
00:01:44,701 --> 00:01:46,800
Yeah, I do.

27
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:50,039
I need to get out more.

28
00:01:50,039 --> 00:01:52,100
Well, I mean

29
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:53,758
there's a lot to do around the house,

30
00:01:53,758 --> 00:01:55,400
and I love being here with the family,

31
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:55,600
you know,

32
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:59,800
but I'm restless.

33
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:01,510
Since I retired,

34
00:02:01,510 --> 00:02:03,600
I've got extra time on my hands.

35
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:06,800
I understand, Grandpa.

36
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:08,600
I think you do.

37
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:10,339
Frankly,

38
00:02:10,339 --> 00:02:13,400
I'd like to use my brain a little more.

39
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,400
Grandpa,

40
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:18,400
you have so much energy and so many years of experience.

41
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:21,084
There are probably a lot of places for you to work

42
00:02:21,084 --> 00:02:23,726
Particularly in the construction field.

43
00:02:23,726 --> 00:02:25,511
But at my age,

44
00:02:25,511 --> 00:02:27,813
I'm not looking for a full-time job.

45
00:02:27,813 --> 00:02:30,700
I'm retired.

46
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:31,300
But I'm bored.

47
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:36,300
Well, there must be something.

48
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:40,500
Maybe I can help.

49
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:42,100
Let's go into the kitchen,

50
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:45,155
and maybe you can help me set the table.

51
00:02:45,155 --> 00:02:46,000
Sounds good to me.

52
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,700
What are we having?

53
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:49,200
I prepared lamb chops,

54
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:52,300
mashed potatoes, and a tossed green salad to begin with.

55
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:54,173
Grandpa, you are a terrific guy!

56
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:54,173
You're still thinking about something to do, aren't you?

57
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:54,173
A job of some kind.

58
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:54,173
That's right.

59
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:54,173
I've been thinking about it for weeks now.

60
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:54,173
There must be some way to put my mind to good use.

61
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:54,173
We'll find a solution.

62
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:54,173
A positive solution

63
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:54,173
to your finding a way to use that wonderful mind of yours.
